# A class beside objects of no known class: the edge of a test cannot keep what the type proves about the class, and its failing edge cannot take the class out of the type.
# The test on the entry of the loop decides the tests in both copies all the same, so a second run finds nothing to place. Behind the passing edge the value is used with what the test and its type say together
